# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v2 SANDBOX — never commit, never deploy.
#
# v2/ is an isolated experiment: a full copy of the dataset plus a retrain
# with hard negatives, kept completely separate from the shipping project.
# It must not reach GitHub or Hugging Face Spaces. If the experiment works we
# promote it deliberately; if it does not, we delete the directory and nothing
# in the live project was ever touched.
#
# To promote v2 later: copy the specific files you want into the root, do NOT
# remove this ignore rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
v2/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded source datasets.
#
# git-push.bat runs `git add .`, so without these rules a finished PlantVillage
# clone (~54,000 images) or an extracted Paddy Doctor archive would be committed
# straight into the repo. Neither belongs in version control - they are inputs
# to v2/scripts/, and v2/ itself is already ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PlantVillage-Dataset/
paddy-doctor/
paddydoc/
train_images/
test_images/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The original training/validation image sets — 5,344 files, 884MB.
#
# Committed long before this rule existed, so .gitignore never applied to them
# and a plain `git add -A` puts every one of them straight back. This rule is a
# second line of defence only: deploy.bat drops them from the index explicitly
# after each `git add`, because this block has already been lost twice when a
# checkout restored an older branch's copy of .gitignore.
#
# They are training inputs. Nothing at runtime reads them, and pushing them to
# a Hugging Face Space gets the push rejected by its pre-receive hook.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
train/
validation/
train_stage2/
validation_stage2/

# Local scratch / diagnostics
bg_test/
*.pdf
diagnose_output.txt

# Test images (now under diagnostics/images/).
#
# Excluded for LICENSING, not size - t2.jpg carries a visible Science Photo
# Library watermark and t1/t3 are of unclear provenance. They are the evidence
# behind the post-mortem, so they are kept locally and referenced in the docs,
# but not redistributed. Anyone reproducing the work should substitute their own
# field photographs; v2/scripts/06_test_real_photos.py accepts any images placed
# in diagnostics/images/.
t1.webp
t2.jpg
t3.jpg

# Node — only present because diagnostics/test_frontend.js needs jsdom.
# package.json and package-lock.json ARE committed so the test is reproducible;
# the 1,840 installed files are not. git-push.bat runs `git add .`, so without
# this rule they go straight into the repo (audit finding A-10).
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Logs
*.log

# Quarantined for manual deletion (sandbox could not rm)
_DELETE_ME/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded v1 weights: 778MB of Stage 1 checkpoints and unused Stage 2
# duplicates, kept locally for comparison but not worth a Git LFS quota that is
# 1GB on the free tier. The live model is in saved_models/stage1_models/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
saved_models/v1_archive/
